cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite the preprint below."
title: "The Anatomy of the CTC Oracle Gap: Acoustic Exhaustion and Linguistic Recovery"
abstract: >-
  Studies where the bottleneck lies in near-converged CTC ASR decoding and
  establishes that it is linguistic rather than acoustic: eleven CTC-internal
  scorers yield no significant WER improvement, while MBR decoding with a RoBERTa
  pseudo-log-likelihood posterior recovers a 9.0% relative WER reduction on
  held-out LibriSpeech test-other. Identifies the CTC backward pass as the
  Rao-Blackwellized REINFORCE estimator (numerically verified).
